{
  "id": "lendloopNotify01",
  "name": "LendLoop 1: Request status notifications",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## LendLoop 1: request status notifications\n\nConvex POSTs here when a borrow request is created or changes status.\n\n1. **Verify**: recompute the HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body and compare it with `X-LendLoop-Signature`; also require `sentAt` (inside the signed body) to be under 5 minutes old. Otherwise answer 401.\n2. **Acknowledge** with 202 so Convex stops retrying.\n3. **De-duplicate** on `eventId` (Convex retries reuse it).\n4. **Validate** the payload shape; a malformed event stops with an error (visible via the error workflow) instead of sending an empty message.\n5. **Notify** the one recipient in the payload: by email through Amazon SES when `LENDLOOP_NOTIFY_CHANNEL=ses` (AWS key held in an n8n credential), otherwise by POSTing to the mock sink, which just logs it.\n6. **Report back** to Convex (signed) so the loan shows \"notification sent\".\n\nConfiguration comes from environment variables, so this export holds no secrets:\n`LENDLOOP_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `LENDLOOP_CONVEX_SITE_URL`, `LENDLOOP_NOTIFY_CHANNEL`, `LENDLOOP_NOTIFY_SINK_URL`, `LENDLOOP_SES_FROM`.\n\nFailures run the \"LendLoop: Error handler\" workflow.",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 440
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a01",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -540,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "lendloop-request-status",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {
          "rawBody": true
        }
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a02",
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "lendloop-request-status"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "action": "hmac",
        "binaryData": true,
        "binaryPropertyName": "data",
        "type": "SHA256",
        "dataPropertyName": "expectedSignature",
        "secret": "={{ $env.LENDLOOP_WEBHOOK_SECRET }}",
        "encoding": "hex"
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a03",
      "name": "HMAC of raw body",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.crypto",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1a5b6f0-0001-4a55-9d0c-5f0b1b525c0e",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.expectedSignature }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $json.headers['x-lendloop-signature'] ?? '' }}",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "c1a5b6f0-0002-4a55-9d0c-5f0b1b525c0e",
              "leftValue": "={{ Math.abs(Date.now() - Number($json.body?.sentAt)) < 300000 }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a04",
      "name": "Signature valid and fresh?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { \"received\": true } }}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 202
        }
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a05",
      "name": "Acknowledge (202)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        680,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { \"error\": \"Invalid or stale signature\" } }}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 401
        }
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a06",
      "name": "Reject (401)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        680,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "removeItemsSeenInPreviousExecutions",
        "dedupeValue": "={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.eventId }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a07",
      "name": "Drop already-seen events",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.removeDuplicates",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        900,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a55d0c1c-0001-4a55-9d0c-5f0b1b525c0e",
              "name": "to",
              "value": "={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.recipient.email ?? '' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a55d0c1c-0002-4a55-9d0c-5f0b1b525c0e",
              "name": "text",
              "value": "={{ ((b) => ({ requested: `Hi ${b.recipient.name}, ${b.counterpartName} would like to borrow your ${b.toolName} from ${b.startDate} to ${b.endDate}.`, accepted: `Hi ${b.recipient.name}, ${b.counterpartName} accepted your request for the ${b.toolName} (${b.startDate} to ${b.endDate}).`, rejected: `Hi ${b.recipient.name}, your request for the ${b.toolName} was declined.`, returned: `Hi ${b.recipient.name}, ${b.counterpartName} marked the ${b.toolName} as returned. Thanks for bringing it back.`, cancelled: `Hi ${b.recipient.name}, ${b.counterpartName} cancelled their request for your ${b.toolName}.` })[b.event] ?? `Hi ${b.recipient.name}, your request for the ${b.toolName} is now ${b.event}.`)($('Webhook').item.json.body) }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a55d0c1c-0003-4a55-9d0c-5f0b1b525c0e",
              "name": "event",
              "value": "={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.event }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a55d0c1c-0006-4a55-9d0c-5f0b1b525c0e",
              "name": "subject",
              "value": "={{ ((b) => ({ requested: `Request to borrow your ${b.toolName}`, accepted: `Your request for the ${b.toolName} was accepted`, rejected: `Your request for the ${b.toolName} was declined`, returned: `${b.toolName} marked as returned`, cancelled: `Request for your ${b.toolName} withdrawn` })[b.event] ?? `LendLoop: ${b.toolName}`)($('Webhook').item.json.body) }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a08",
      "name": "Build notification",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1340,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.LENDLOOP_NOTIFY_SINK_URL }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ to: $json.to, text: $json.text, event: $json.event }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 10000
        }
      },
      "id": "5f0b1b52-5c0e-4a55-9d0c-1c1a5b6f0a09",
      "name": "Log to mock sink",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1780,
        0
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 3000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a55d0c1c-0004-4a55-9d0c-5f0b1b525c0e",
              "name": "timestamp",
              "value": "={{ Date.now().toString() }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a55d0c1c-0005-4a55-9d0c-5f0b1b525c0e",
